From: harlan <hmccanne@exclamationpoint.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ncsi: demote benign rsp validation/handler logs to debug

During normal NCSI channel/package negotiation the controller legitimately
emits responses that fail ncsi_rcv_rsp()'s validation (e.g. Set VLAN Filter,
type 0x8b) or that a per-command handler rejects (e.g. a Deselect Package
response, type 0x82, for a package/channel the host has already torn down,
which ncsi_rsp_handler_dp() reports as -ENODEV).  The NCSI state machine
recovers from both on its own, but the two messages are logged at warn/err
level and flood the kernel log on every boot across the fleet.

Demote both to netdev_dbg so they no longer appear in dmesg by default while
remaining available via dynamic debug.  No functional change.
---
 net/ncsi/ncsi-rsp.c | 8 ++++----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

--- a/net/ncsi/ncsi-rsp.c
+++ b/net/ncsi/ncsi-rsp.c
@@ -1198,9 +1198,9 @@
 		payload = ntohs(hdr->length);
 	ret = ncsi_validate_rsp_pkt(nr, payload);
 	if (ret) {
-		netdev_warn(ndp->ndev.dev,
-			    "NCSI: 'bad' packet ignored for type 0x%x\n",
-			    hdr->type);
+		netdev_dbg(ndp->ndev.dev,
+			   "NCSI: 'bad' packet ignored for type 0x%x\n",
+			   hdr->type);
 
 		if (nr->flags == NCSI_REQ_FLAG_NETLINK_DRIVEN) {
 			if (ret == -EPERM)
@@ -1218,7 +1218,7 @@
 	/* Process the packet */
 	ret = nrh->handler(nr);
 	if (ret)
-		netdev_err(ndp->ndev.dev,
+		netdev_dbg(ndp->ndev.dev,
 			   "NCSI: Handler for packet type 0x%x returned %d\n",
 			   hdr->type, ret);
 
